  "statementMd": "`board` is a 9x9 grid of single-character strings (digits or `\".\"` for empty). Return whether the filled cells obey the rules: no repeated digit in any row, column or 3x3 box.\n\n**Example:** `valid_sudoku([[\"5\", \"3\", \".\", \".\", \"7\", \".\", \".\", \".\", \".\"], [\"6\", \".\", …)` returns `true`.",
  "hints": [
    "Track seen sets per row, column and box."
  ],
  "solutionMd": "```python\ndef valid_sudoku(board):\n    seen = set()\n    for r in range(9):\n        for c in range(9):\n            v = board[r][c]\n            if v == '.':\n                continue\n            keys = [('r', r, v), ('c', c, v), ('b', r // 3, c // 3, v)]\n            if any(k in seen for k in keys):\n                return False\n            seen.update(keys)\n    return True\n```\n\nOne set with tagged keys is enough.",
